# Voltage and branch-power figures

Register each figure in 01_IDEA/figure_plan.md. Show the original physical quantity, units, matched cases and actual methods.

MC full AC histogram is the reference background. Overlay the actual TMM semi-analytical PDF/CDF; if a curve comes from model-only sampling, label it separately. Preserve bins, counts, range mass, grid, numerical checks, seeds, source/model hashes and actual command.

Keep fixed-voltage and fixed-output atoms explicit. Do not smooth away point mass, clip model samples, alter data, remove bad states or invent curves.

Report full tables across buses and branch ends. Representative plots do not replace complete statistics. Mean/standard-deviation/quantile/CDF errors and MC uncertainty accompany visual comparisons. Do not call grid CDF error exact KS.

Use independent subfigures and readable legends/units, with color and line style together. Cloud Python plots are authorized. Formal export requires actual data; planning records or network inputs are not plot evidence.

PowerLit is unavailable in this session. Record the fallback once and review nearby primary papers before formal figure export; do not add new parameter studies to fill a template slot.
